  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user waiting for a list, I want the loading state to be the plain system indicator, or to say something specific, so that the five list screens load the same way.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"If it's helpful, display a description that provides additional context for the task. Be accurate and succinct. Avoid vague terms like loading or authenticating because they seldom add value.\" — [HIG › Progress indicators](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/progress-indicators) (Best practices; page updated 2023-09-12).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/QualityAlerts/QualityAlertsView.swift:75` `ProgressView(\"Chargement…\")`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListView.swift:300` `ProgressView(\"Chargement des sujets\")`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Messages/MessageListView.swift:89` `ProgressView(\"Chargement des messages\")`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Profile/UserProfileView.swift:73` `ProgressView(\"Chargement du profil…\")`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/FilteredPosts/FilteredPostsView.swift:104`\n\nTwo end with « … », three do not. A specific caption exists and is fine: « Recherche des MP multiples » (`MessageListView.swift:79`).\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\n`HFRswift/Swift/AQPlusView.swift:387` `ProgressView(\"Chargement...\")` (same); `Favorites.swift:1231` and `UserProfileView.swift:571` use an unlabelled `ProgressView()`: SwiftHFR added the captions on topics and profile.\n\n### Class\n\n**(b) evolution, M5** (wording, no accessibility impact: VoiceOver announces the indicator either way).\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- A bare `ProgressView()` for full-screen first loads, through the shared state component of #693; keep a caption only where it says something specific.\n- Check: text review; the first load of each list on the next device review (#893).\n\nRelated: #693 (shared state components).\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
